<title>CHINA: China stockbrokers told not to use private funds.</title>
<headline>China stockbrokers told not to use private funds.</headline>
<dateline>SHANGHAI 1996-11-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Shanghai Stock Exchange has instructed its members not to allow institutions to use private accounts which are held only for private investors, the China Securities newspaper said on Friday.</p>
<p>In a recent instruction, the exchange also said that private investors were not allowed to use institutional accounts to trade stocks.</p>
<p>Some domestic institutions are using private accounts to speculate in stocks in order to evade official supervision, analysts said.</p>
</text>
